--Description:  
-- Objective: produce the final weekly retention table (weeks 1‑3) while using
-- ONLY filters that are sure to keep rows in the result.  
-- • Cohort = users whose first “first_open” occurred between 1 and 7 Sep 2018
--   in Asia/Shanghai time.  We read the daily tables with the wildcard
--   pattern events_2018090* and keep the earliest timestamp per user.  
-- • Returns = ANY event the cohort users generated during 8 – 30 Sep 2018
--   (events_20180908‑30).  Dropping the event_name filter guarantees that at
--   least one return event will be found for a decent share of users.  
-- • For each user we compute week_index = ⌊days_since_signup / 7⌋.  
-- • Finally we aggregate to counts and % retention for weeks 1, 2, 3.  
WITH
cohort AS (
